WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.508 --> 00:00:02.273
-Thank you so much
for being here, bud.

00:00:02.273 --> 00:00:04.634
It's always good to talk to you.
I wanted to say,

00:00:04.634 --> 00:00:06.133
before we even
get into the interview,

00:00:06.133 --> 00:00:10.667
how great you were on --
I watched the Mike Tyson Triller

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:13.267
boxing --
the match where you were there.

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:15.934
You were a commentator,
but you also performed.

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:17.968
And you stole the show
for me, dude.

00:00:17.968 --> 00:00:19.901
You were unbelievable.
Everything top-notch.

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:22.200
-We had a great time too, Jimmy.
It was a great night.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.467
It was a coming-out night
for me, basically.

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:26.701
A lot of people knew
that I was doing that.

00:00:26.701 --> 00:00:28.467
But to be on that stage,
and to be able

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.367
to pull it off
in front of the whole world.

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:32.267
Now we're doing one
on April 17th,

00:00:32.267 --> 00:00:34.934
which is a follow-Up fight,
and it's very well produced.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.334
We got a lot of great acts
performing.

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:39.501
Big fights that night.
April 17th, we doing it again.

00:00:39.501 --> 00:00:41.367
-Yeah, I want to talk to you
about that.

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:44.000
First, also, I want to give you
props on your jacket.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:46.634
That's your --
That's "Doggystyle."

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:49.067
That's your first --
That's your first record.

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:52.000
-Yeah, that's the jacket that's
on The Snoopermarket right now.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.667
If y'all want to go to
snoopermarket.com,

00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:55.334
y'all can pick up one.
You understand me?

00:00:55.334 --> 00:01:00.133
-That's my home page.
-Yeah, Snoopermarket, baby.

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:01.601
Come get you some.
-Yeah, Snoopermarket.

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:03.234
That's my -- I use that
more than Google, man.

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:04.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:07.367
You've worked with so many great
artists throughout your career.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:13.400
Obviously, the great DMX, sadly,
passed away on Friday.

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:17.634
I know you worked with him.
The last thing I saw,

00:01:17.634 --> 00:01:19.901
you guys were doing
the Verzuz Battle.

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:23.167
What did it mean for to you
to share the stage with him?

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:26.701
-It meant the world because
it gave the world a chance

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:29.501
to see two dogs
that naturally love each other

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:32.067
celebrate each other
in the name of hip-hop.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:36.334
You're seeing a lot of,
interaction between me and him,

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:38.133
engaging in our songs.

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:40.300
You're seeing a lot of
conversations and a lot of love.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.734
And we had God in the building
with us that night.

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:45.834
And that makes me feel good
about DMX's transition

00:01:45.834 --> 00:01:47.834
to know that he's
off to a better place

00:01:47.834 --> 00:01:49.567
and he's finally got
his angel wings.

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:52.133
-Yeah.
When did you first meet him?

00:01:52.133 --> 00:01:54.200
Do you remember?

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.234
-At a concert
at Trafalgar Square.

00:01:57.234 --> 00:02:01.434
19 -- I think it was like, '94.

00:02:01.434 --> 00:02:04.200
And then we went back
to the studio after that.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.567
That was the first time
I actually met DMX.

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:10.834
-What comes to mind when you
think about that -- that night?

00:02:10.834 --> 00:02:14.667
-He brought up a story
that was so -- so -- so deep

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.534
and instrumental
to our relationship.

00:02:16.534 --> 00:02:19.200
He was like, "When you first met
me, I was, like, away from Him.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.400
And He was saying,
'What's happening? What's up?'

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.868
And I was like,
'Get at me, dog.'"

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:25.801
He was like, "I took that and
I made that into my song,

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:28.167
'Get At Me Dog.'
'cause the way you got at me

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:29.834
and said that,
I was like, 'That's slick.'"

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:32.300
So, that night inspired him

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.033
to create that song
"Get At Me Dog,"

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:37.300
which was one of his biggest
hood records that he put out.

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.968
-Oh, my gosh.
I appreciate you talking to us

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:43.167
about this.
I know it just happened.

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:45.300
So thank you very much
for doing that.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:47.234
And we're gonna miss him.
-Jimmy, it's what we do.

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:49.501
We keep hip-hop alive,
and legends never die.

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:52.033
Their soul will continue
to, you know, bless the world.

00:02:52.033 --> 00:02:53.634
And he was a great,
you know, spirit.

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:55.501
He always
looked out for everybody.

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:59.767
He always prayed for everybody,
So now we can finally say

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:02.033
he got his angel wings and
he's off to a better place.

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:03.734
-That's what I'm talking about.
Thanks, man.

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:05.434
[ Applause ]

00:03:05.434 --> 00:03:08.667
Something that I've always
loved about you is

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:13.067
not only your work
as a great hip-hop legend,

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:14.934
but you're also --
as a businessman.

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:17.968
You're always working on
something brand-new.

00:03:17.968 --> 00:03:21.234
I want to say,
probably twice a year,

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:24.100
I get a nice gift from you,
and I appreciate it.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.501
I get -- I think the last thing
I received was a gin --

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:29.834
a juice-flavored gin --
with beautiful cups.

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:31.834
Of course, gin and juice --
you got to do that.

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:34.767
-Yeah, that's my company.
INDOGGO Gin.

00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:37.968
-You've now started
a boxing league with Triller,

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:41.000
called Fight Club.
And this Saturday, big fight.

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:42.767
What is the fight
happening on Saturday?

00:03:42.767 --> 00:03:46.601
-Jake Paul versus Ben Askren.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:48.501
This is gonna be a great fight
because there's been

00:03:48.501 --> 00:03:50.234
